<div class="kicker"><a href="/">Follow the Money</a> · Straw poll</div>
<h1>Build Your 2028 Dream <em>Ticket</em></h1>
<div class="standfirst">The 2028 race is already surfacing — earlier than anyone expected. Build a ticket — President and VP — then rank up to three. Every card is sourced; nobody's here because we made them up.</div>
<div class="meta">{{ ticket2028.race }} · updated {{ ticket2028.updated }} &nbsp;·&nbsp; anonymous · no login</div>

<div class="ticket-slots" id="ticketSlots">
  <div class="slot" id="slot-pres"><span class="slot-role">President</span><span class="slot-name" id="pres-name">— pick one —</span></div>
  <div class="slot-x">+</div>
  <div class="slot" id="slot-vp"><span class="slot-role">Vice President</span><span class="slot-name" id="vp-name">— pick one —</span></div>
</div>
<div class="ticket-actions">
  <button class="start-btn" id="addTicket" type="button" disabled onclick="addToBallot()">＋ Add to my ranked list</button>
</div>

<div class="ballot">
  <div class="ballot-h">My top three <span class="ballot-hint">rank up to three — your 1st choice counts most</span></div>
  <ol class="ballot-list" id="ballotList"></ol>
  <div class="ticket-actions">
    <button class="start-btn" id="submitBallot" type="button" disabled onclick="submitBallot()">Submit my ballot</button>
    <button class="start-btn again" id="shareTicket" type="button" onclick="shareTicket()" style="display:none">📤 Share my ballot</button>
    <button class="start-btn again" id="changeTicket" type="button" onclick="changeBallot()" style="display:none">↺ Change my ballot</button>
    <div class="ticket-share-row" id="ticketShareRow"></div>
    <div class="locked-note" id="lockedNote" style="display:none">✓ Ballot locked for this browser — you can change it anytime.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="cand-grid">
{%- for c in ticket2028.candidates %}
  <div class="cand" data-id="{{ c.id }}">
    <div class="cand-head"><span class="cand-name">{{ c.name }}</span><span class="cand-lane">{{ c.lane }}</span></div>
    {%- if c.caveat %}<div class="cand-flag">⚑ {{ c.caveat }}</div>{% endif %}
    <ul class="cand-facts">
    {%- for f in c.facts %}
      <li>{{ f.text }} <a href="{{ f.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">— {{ f.label }} ↗</a></li>
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    <div class="cand-pick">
      <button class="pick-btn pick-pres" type="button" onclick="pick('pres','{{ c.id }}')">★ President</button>
      <button class="pick-btn pick-vp" type="button" onclick="pick('vp','{{ c.id }}')">☆ VP</button>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>

<div class="sourcing-note">These names are drawn from public polling and party/advocate chatter as of {{ ticket2028.updated }}. Every fact links to its source; a <span class="cand-caveat">⚑</span> marks candidates who haven't committed to running (Ossoff and Whitmer have said no). This is an <strong>unscientific straw poll</strong>, not an endorsement or a prediction — one ballot per browser, and like any open poll it measures enthusiasm, not electorates.</div>

<h2>How the country's ranking them</h2>
<div class="borda-note"><strong>How the ranking works — it's a Borda count.</strong> A ranked-voting method: your <b>1st choice earns 3 points</b>, your <b>2nd earns 2</b>, your <b>3rd earns 1</b>, and we total them across every ballot. It rewards tickets with <em>broad</em> support, not just the loudest first-place fans — the same idea behind ranked-choice voting reforms. <a href="https://fairvote.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn how ranked voting works ↗</a></div>
<div class="leaderboard" id="leaderboard"><p class="lb-empty">Loading the standings…</p></div>

<h2>How we count (and what we don't keep)</h2>
<p>Your ballot never becomes a record of <em>you</em>. Here's exactly what happens, and why we built it this way:</p>
<div class="receipts"><ul>
  <li><span>No cookies, no login, no tracking</span><span class="receipt-srcs">nothing follows you between visits or sites</span></li>
  <li><span>Each ranked pick is one anonymous tally mark</span><span class="receipt-srcs">a pairing like "harris / kelly" — no name, no time, no IP, no session</span></li>
  <li><span>It lives in append-only storage, not a database of people</span><span class="receipt-srcs">there is no row that is "you" to leak, join, or subpoena</span></li>
  <li><span>Your browser remembers only your own ballot</span><span class="receipt-srcs">locally, so you can't double-vote and can change your mind — never sent to us</span></li>
  <li><span>Do Not Track is honored</span><span class="receipt-srcs">if your browser sets it, we send nothing at all</span></li>
</ul></div>
<p class="sourcing-note">In short: we can show that "N people ranked this pairing," but we can never show that <em>you</em> did. That's a property of the design, not a promise you have to trust. Full detail on our <a href="/legal">privacy page</a>.</p>

<h2>The receipts</h2>
<p>Every figure above is public — polling and campaign-finance disclosures. Check them yourself:</p>
<div class="receipts"><ul>
{%- for c in ticket2028.candidates %}
  <li><span>{{ c.short }}</span><span class="receipt-srcs">
  {%- for f in c.facts %}
    <a href="{{ f.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ f.label }} ↗</a>
  {%- endfor %}
  </span></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul></div>

<div class="float-bar" id="floatBar" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="float-pick" id="floatPick"></span>
  <button class="float-btn add" id="floatAdd" type="button" onclick="addToBallot()">＋ Add to ranked list</button>
  <button class="float-btn submit" id="floatSubmit" type="button" onclick="submitBallot()">Submit ballot</button>
</div>

<script>window.__TICKET = { {% for c in ticket2028.candidates %}"{{ c.id }}": "{{ c.short }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };</script>
